# OPUS-ROOT-CALL-20260930-17: `Model: Other extra`, both arguments known, is Model's two-argument call -- refused at
# its own line.  A named Structure is no type word: `Model: a b` declares nothing (a named Structure T declares only
# by `T: name`, as in a method).  The classifier took the registered Model for one, so the lexical pass's count walk
# (nothing registered) and fill walk (Model registered) disagreed about `Other:` and the fill wrote a statement past
# E's counted fields: this program crashed the translator (STATUS_HEAP_CORRUPTION).
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

Other:
    size_t: p 2U
end: Other

int: extra 1
Model: Other extra
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
